  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 951 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nA trough will move out of the Rockies this weekend, bringing \nmedium rain chances around 40-50% to all of Middle Tennessee late\nSunday. Instability looks slim to none, so not expecting much in \nthe way of thunderstorms; 10% chance or less. The lack of \ninstability will also result in unimpressive rainfall amounts of \ngenerally a tenth of an inch or less. A quarter-inch may be \npossible for those near the Tennessee River, but that looks to be \nabout the highest we'd see. A cold front will usher in behind \nthese showers, dropping temperatures back into the 50s for highs \nand 30s to upper 20s for lows next week. As such, Monday and \nTuesday will be cool, breezy, and dry. We'll have another chance \nfor rain on Wednesday, though models are still struggling with the\neventual path the upper low will take. Most members of both the \nGEFS and ECMWF ensembles are favoring rain, resulting in an \nincrease for rain chances on Wednesday to 40-60%. Given the \nuncertainty of the low's track, QPF amounts remain a bit more \nuncertain. Thanksgiving Day continues to trend dry, but cool with \nhighs around 50 and lows in the mid to upper 20s.",
